claim.claim-text:
determining (201) a reference signal resource used for sending the reference signal; and
sending (202) the reference signal by using the determined reference signal resource;
wherein the reference signal resource comprises a frequency domain resource, and the frequency domain resource used for sending the reference signal is determined according to a transmission comb index of the reference signal;
wherein the second processor (401) is configured to further implement: in a case where the reference signal comprises reference signals of a plurality of ports, determining transmission comb indexes used by the reference signals of the plurality of ports, respectively; wherein the second processor (401) is configured to implement determining the transmission comb indexes used by the reference signals of the plurality of ports, respectively, by:
in a case where a transmission comb index configured by the reference signal resource is k, determining that a transmission comb index used by a reference signal of at least one predefined port in the plurality of ports is k, and determining that each of transmission comb indexes used by reference signals of remaining ports is one of k or mod(k+ KTC/2, KTC); wherein mod is a modulus function, and KTC is a number of transmission combs of the reference signal;
wherein the second processor (401) is configured to further implement: receiving the reference signal resource configured through signaling; wherein the second processor (401) is configured to implement receiving the reference signal resource configured through the signaling by:
receiving a plurality of reference signal resources through the signaling; wherein a time domain guard interval among the plurality of reference signal resources is Y time domain symbols, and a manner for determining a value of Y comprises: predetermining different values of Y for different subcarrier spacings; wherein predetermining the different values of Y for the different subcarrier spacings comprises at least one of:
in a case where a configuration of a subcarrier spacing is 0 or a subcarrier spacing is 15 KHz, predetermining the value of Y as 1;
in a case where a configuration of a subcarrier spacing is 1 or a subcarrier spacing is 30 KHz, predetermining the value of Y as 1;
in a case where a configuration of a subcarrier spacing is 2 or a subcarrier spacing is 60 KHz, predetermining the value of Y as 1;
in a case where a configuration of a subcarrier spacing is 3 or a subcarrier spacing is 120 KHz, predetermining the value of Y as 2; or
in a case where a configuration of a subcarrier spacing is 4 or a subcarrier spacing is 240 KHz, predetermining the value of Y as 4;

determining (201), by a user equipment, UE, a reference signal resource used for sending the reference signal; and
sending (202), by the UE, the reference signal by using the determined reference signal resource;
wherein the reference signal resource comprises a frequency domain resource, and the frequency domain resource used for sending the reference signal is determined according to a transmission comb index of the reference signal;
wherein the method further comprises: in a case where the reference signal comprises reference signals of a plurality of ports, determining, by the UE, transmission comb indexes used by the reference signals of the plurality of ports, respectively; wherein determining, by the UE, the transmission comb indexes used by the reference signals of the plurality of ports, respectively comprises:
in a case where a transmission comb index configured by the reference signal resource is k, determining that a transmission comb index used by a reference signal of at least one predefined port in the plurality of ports is k, and determining that each of transmission comb indexes used by reference signals of remaining ports is one of k or mod(k+ KTC/2, KTC); wherein mod is a modulus function, and KTC is a number of transmission combs of the reference signal;
wherein the method further comprises: receiving, by the UE, the reference signal resource configured through signaling; wherein receiving, by the UE, the reference signal resource configured through the signaling comprises:
receiving a plurality of reference signal resources through the signaling; wherein a time domain guard interval among the plurality of reference signal resources is Y time domain symbols, and a manner for determining a value of Y comprises: predetermining different values of Y for different subcarrier spacings; wherein predetermining the different values of Y for the different subcarrier spacings comprises at least one of:
in a case where a configuration of a subcarrier spacing is 0 or a subcarrier spacing is 15 KHz, predetermining the value of Y as 1;
in a case where a configuration of a subcarrier spacing is 1 or a subcarrier spacing is 30 KHz, predetermining the value of Y as 1;
in a case where a configuration of a subcarrier spacing is 2 or a subcarrier spacing is 60 KHz, predetermining the value of Y as 1;
in a case where a configuration of a subcarrier spacing is 3 or a subcarrier spacing is 120 KHz, predetermining the value of Y as 2; or
in a case where a configuration of a subcarrier spacing is 4 or a subcarrier spacing is 240 KHz, predetermining the value of Y as 4;

